menu "PQC Secure Boot"

    config PQC_SECURE_BOOT_ENABLED
        bool "Enable PQC (ML-DSA-65) signature verification in bootloader"
        default y
        depends on SECURE_BOOT_V2_ENABLED && !SECURE_SIGNED_APPS_ECDSA_SCHEME
        help
            When enabled, the bootloader verifies the ML-DSA-65 PQC signature
            block (located immediately after the 4 KB RSA/ECDSA V2 signature block
            in flash) BEFORE performing RSA or ECDSA V2 Secure Boot V2 verification.
            Both checks must pass for the image to be loaded.

            Supported scheme: RSA-PSS 3072-bit (ESP32-C3/C5/C6).
            Not compatible with legacy ECDSA V1 scheme (SECURE_SIGNED_APPS_ECDSA_SCHEME).

            When disabled, only the standard RSA/ECDSA V2 Secure Boot V2 verification
            is performed — identical to unmodified ESP-IDF behaviour.

    choice PQC_MEMORY_STRATEGY
        prompt "PQC memory management strategy"
        depends on PQC_SECURE_BOOT_ENABLED
        default PQC_MEM_TLSF
        help
            Choose how ML-DSA-65 internal buffers are allocated during
            signature verification in the bootloader.

        config PQC_MEM_STACK
            bool "Stack (buffers on dedicated 80KB PQC stack)"
            help
                All ML-DSA-65 intermediate buffers are stack-allocated on
                the dedicated 80KB PQC stack reserved permanently in
                bootloader dram_seg. Simple, zero fragmentation, but costs
                ~80KB of app SRAM permanently.

        config PQC_MEM_TLSF
            bool "TLSF Heap (temporary app SRAM region)"
            help
                ML-DSA-65 buffers are dynamically allocated from a TLSF pool
                placed at a fixed address in the bottom of the app's SRAM
                (0x40800000). The bootloader borrows this region during
                verification, zeroes it afterwards, and the app reclaims it
                as heap — saving ~80KB of SRAM for the application.
                PQC call-frame stack is reduced to 8KB (call frames only).

    endchoice

    config PQC_TLSF_POOL_SIZE_KB
        int "TLSF pool size in KB"
        depends on PQC_MEM_TLSF
        default 48
        range 32 128
        help
            Size of the TLSF pool placed at PQC_TEMP_REGION_ADDR in app SRAM.
            ML-DSA-65 verify needs ~35KB peak. 48KB provides ~13KB headroom.

    config PQC_CALL_STACK_SIZE_KB
        int "PQC call-frame stack size in KB"
        depends on PQC_MEM_TLSF
        default 8
        range 4 16
        help
            Size of the PQC call-frame stack placed immediately after the
            TLSF pool in the temporary region. 8KB provides >4x headroom
            over the measured ~1.6KB maximum call depth.

    config PQC_MLD_REDUCE_RAM
        bool "Enable ML-DSA REDUCE_RAM optimizations"
        depends on PQC_SECURE_BOOT_ENABLED
        default y
        help
            When enabled, ML-DSA-65 uses row-buffer matrix multiplication
            and serial FIPS-202 hashing, reducing peak RAM from ~30KB to ~5KB
            at the cost of slower verification.

            Disable this to use the full-speed implementation and measure
            the actual RAM difference.

    config PQC_DEBUG_VERBOSE
        bool "Enable verbose PQC debug prints"
        depends on PQC_SECURE_BOOT_ENABLED
        default n
        help
            When enabled, prints detailed debug information during PQC
            verification: TLSF heap pointers and allocation sizes, PQC
            stack region addresses, PQC block header fields, and
            step-by-step verification progress.

            Useful for performance profiling and debugging memory issues.
            Disable for production builds to reduce boot time and log noise.

endmenu
